node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
# Paired with **/dist above, and load-bearing on the DEFAULT path: `npm run
# docker` builds the local tree, which has these files. A copied-in
# .tsbuildinfo tells `tsc -b` the build is already up to date, so
# @easydb/shared emits no dist/ and the renderer build can't resolve it.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.claude
e2e
# Not a bare `docs` exclusion: vite.config.ts's `gen-tips` buildStart hook
# compiles docs/help/tips.md into the renderer bundle, so that one file has to
# stay reachable. Same /* + ! trick as packages/* below.
docs/*
!docs/help
test-results
playwright-report
# Excluded via /* (not a bare dir match) so the tree stays walkable and the
# Dockerfile can still explicitly re-include just the package.json it needs
# for npm workspaces resolution (a bare "packages/electron" pattern would
# make Docker skip the whole subtree, and the "!" negation below would not
# be able to bring package.json back).
packages/electron/*
!packages/electron/package.json
packages/server/*
!packages/server/package.json
*.log
.vscode
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
